WEBVTT

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:21.500
Those Snow

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:21.500
White Notes

00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:35.430
<i>Why am I here, playing like this?</i>

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:38.270
<i>I was aiming for Gramps' sound...</i>

00:01:38.850 --> 00:01:42.760
<i>And here in my first competition,
people want Gramps' sound.</i>

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:45.420
Who are you trying to imitate?

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:50.340
Is that your sound?

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:51.250
Setsu.

00:01:52.010 --> 00:01:55.680
Use your own sound to steal my sound.

00:01:57.360 --> 00:01:59.180
<i>I know, Gramps.</i>

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:04.640
<i>It's only an inkling, but I think I've
found the road home to my sound.</i>

00:02:15.270 --> 00:02:16.270
<i>His sound...</i>

00:02:16.670 --> 00:02:17.770
<i>It's changed.</i>

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:30.670
This sound...

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:33.180
<i>It's like he's a completely
different person now.</i>

00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:37.430
Incredible...

00:02:40.710 --> 00:02:43.440
<i>The sound's filling the whole auditorium.</i>

00:02:43.950 --> 00:02:47.760
<i>Leisurely and serene,
like the tinkling of a little bell...</i>

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:52.240
<i>What a beautiful sound...</i>

00:02:54.850 --> 00:02:57.480
<i>It's just like in the group competition.</i>

00:02:58.010 --> 00:03:00.720
<i>What is this tranquility
that rises up in an instant?</i>

00:03:02.970 --> 00:03:04.070
<i>The rain...</i>

00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:06.080
<i>...has lifted.</i>

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:14.590
<i>I don't need boring sounds.</i>

00:03:15.150 --> 00:03:18.450
<i>What I want right now is the
resonance of the three strings.</i>

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:21.260
<i>What I want to play right now...</i>

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:22.840
<i>What I want people to hear...</i>

00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:26.000
<i>...is a sound with depth.</i>

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:35.620
<i>Everyone has memories... and feelings...</i>

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:37.900
<i>Ah...</i>

00:03:38.990 --> 00:03:40.860
<i>I hope I can get this across.</i>

00:03:41.390 --> 00:03:43.130
<i>Everyone...</i>

00:03:43.130 --> 00:03:44.600
<i>I hope this reaches you.</i>

00:03:46.170 --> 00:03:47.290
<i>What is this?</i>

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:55.790
<i>Why are these distant memories
resurfacing after all this time?</i>

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:08.140
<i>I see. This feeling...</i>

00:04:09.630 --> 00:04:10.850
<i>...is called yearning.</i>

00:04:12.220 --> 00:04:14.940
<i>Setsu! Why are you playing that sound?!</i>

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:18.400
That's the way.

00:04:19.110 --> 00:04:21.900
We've played together since we were little,

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:25.480
so I know that "having fun" is your sound.

00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:27.600
<i>Sawamura-kun!</i>

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:29.500
It's Setsu-san's sound!

00:04:31.490 --> 00:04:33.500
<i>Ever since I first heard you play,</i>

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:36.690
<i>I've thought you were on a
different plane to the rest of us.</i>

00:04:37.370 --> 00:04:40.380
<i>Your sound...
is the sound of a beating heart.</i>

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:45.720
<i>You really are...</i>

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:49.500
That'sвЂ”

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:50.220
So fast!

00:04:55.850 --> 00:04:57.650
Wow! That's amazing, Setsu-kun!

00:04:57.650 --> 00:04:58.690
Land the finish.

00:04:59.100 --> 00:05:01.820
<i>Oh... it's going to end.</i>

00:05:03.230 --> 00:05:04.200
<i>It's over.</i>

00:05:29.260 --> 00:05:32.770
That was amazing! You're amazing!

00:05:32.770 --> 00:05:34.890
Sawamura, you're the best!

00:05:34.890 --> 00:05:37.040
I'm gonna give you such a big hug!

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:39.280
Oh, I hate this! It's so bad for my heart!

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:41.430
It was incredible! It was so good!

00:05:41.430 --> 00:05:42.780
Simply splendid.

00:05:44.430 --> 00:05:46.610
Th-This cheering's insane.

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:48.470
It was so good!

00:05:48.470 --> 00:05:49.320
Wasn't it?

00:05:49.850 --> 00:05:51.840
Yeah. It was good.

00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:53.880
I'm glad I got to hear Setsu's sound.

00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:58.160
<i>So this is Sawamura Setsu?</i>

00:05:58.780 --> 00:06:02.170
<i>I'll admit that I'm interested in
your as-yet-unknown abilities.</i>

00:06:02.860 --> 00:06:05.400
<i>But right now, all I want
to do is play the shamisen.</i>

00:06:06.610 --> 00:06:10.870
<i>I was totally lost in the
resonance of the three strings,</i>

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:13.550
<i>and the vibrations coming
through my chest and into my gut.</i>

00:06:14.060 --> 00:06:15.840
<i>I was able to play a good sound.</i>

00:06:17.530 --> 00:06:18.860
<i>Gramps...</i>

00:06:18.860 --> 00:06:22.610
It's the reactions of the people listening
that are the most important lessons.

00:06:23.170 --> 00:06:24.610
<i>They really are.</i>

00:06:29.130 --> 00:06:30.620
<i>The atmosphere's weird.</i>

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:36.350
<i>It's tense, but sort of bored.
And this guy's giving a stiff performance.</i>

00:06:36.350 --> 00:06:39.370
<i>Everyone's still basking in the
afterglow of Sawamura's performance.</i>

00:06:40.020 --> 00:06:43.760
<i>This is fun. That's my friend for you.</i>

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:48.680
Good work out there.
That was a nice performance.

00:06:48.680 --> 00:06:49.730
Good work.

00:06:49.750 --> 00:06:50.840
Thanks.

00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:54.470
Now comes the final performance.
Tanuma Souichi's taking to the stage.

00:06:56.510 --> 00:06:57.890
<i>Contestant Number 40.</i>

00:06:57.890 --> 00:07:02.300
<i>From Aoba Daiichi High School of
Aomori Prefecture: Tanuma Souichi-kun.</i>

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:04.380
Tanuma?

00:07:04.380 --> 00:07:06.780
He was the runner-up in the
A-level division at Hirosaki.

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:09.200
Is he someone famous?

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:11.100
In this world, yeah.

00:07:11.100 --> 00:07:13.040
He's famous for being eccentric, too.

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:18.040
<i>I haven't heard him play since the
Hirosaki Tournament four months ago.</i>

00:07:21.460 --> 00:07:25.210
You're unlikely to beat
Souichi as you are now.

00:07:26.230 --> 00:07:28.980
<i>I had the neck replaned.</i>

00:07:29.750 --> 00:07:31.360
<i>I also had the skin replaced.</i>

00:07:32.090 --> 00:07:33.560
<i>The strings are new.</i>

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:37.960
<i>And I picked a bachi with a
hardness that suits this piece.</i>

00:07:39.040 --> 00:07:40.970
<i>We're in the best possible condition.</i>

00:07:42.190 --> 00:07:44.640
<i>My instrument is like a part of my body.</i>

00:08:00.460 --> 00:08:03.950
<i>His arm movements are large,
but there isn't even a hint of a wobble.</i>

00:08:04.420 --> 00:08:09.340
<i>He presses his thumb to the skin to deaden
the sound. His tone control is outstanding.</i>

00:08:09.340 --> 00:08:12.490
<i>That leads to strong dynamics in his sound.</i>

00:08:15.420 --> 00:08:17.770
The atmosphere's changed.
They're on his side now.

00:08:19.490 --> 00:08:22.270
<i>First, Souichi draws people
in and wins them over.</i>

00:08:22.270 --> 00:08:23.150
<i>Then...</i>

00:08:35.130 --> 00:08:39.490
<i>He holds his breath and, with arms primed,
he strikes as if awakening from something.</i>

00:08:40.090 --> 00:08:42.030
<i>Much like a sprinter.</i>

00:08:42.460 --> 00:08:46.540
<i>His impassioned sound
uplifts everyone who hears it.</i>

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:49.540
<i>That's Tanuma Souichi.</i>

00:08:51.560 --> 00:08:54.040
<i>WhaвЂ” Hold up.</i>

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:56.650
<i>Th-This is scary.</i>

00:08:56.890 --> 00:08:59.560
<i>He flips swiftly between
fierce and gentle sounds.</i>

00:09:00.040 --> 00:09:02.070
<i>And it all meshes together
with his playfulness!</i>

00:09:02.910 --> 00:09:07.220
<i>It's been four months since Hirosaki...
He's grown so much in just four months!</i>

00:09:07.220 --> 00:09:09.290
<i>How is that even possible?!</i>

00:09:16.190 --> 00:09:18.910
<i>I can't take it. My brain's trembling.</i>

00:09:18.910 --> 00:09:21.500
<i>Hearing it live is totally
different from watching vids!</i>

00:09:21.500 --> 00:09:23.840
<i>The whole venue's shaking.</i>

00:09:24.060 --> 00:09:27.600
<i>It's like having a giant taiko
drum beaten right in front of me.</i>

00:09:28.060 --> 00:09:34.000
<i>I know that, no matter the situation, that
boy always performs to his usual standard.</i>

00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:35.080
<i>Either that, or...</i>

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:39.640
<i>Yes, he might even surpass his usual standard.</i>

00:09:40.380 --> 00:09:43.740
<i>The distinguishing trait of the
Kamiki style is its powerful strikes.</i>

00:09:43.740 --> 00:09:46.570
<i>However, that's all it is, a trait.</i>

00:09:47.040 --> 00:09:50.400
<i>Souichi is building his own sound on top.</i>

00:09:51.260 --> 00:09:53.280
<i>His evolution cannot be stopped.</i>

00:09:59.640 --> 00:10:00.970
<i>The sound...</i>

00:10:00.970 --> 00:10:03.630
<i>It's ricocheting around the
auditorium and swirling together.</i>

00:10:03.910 --> 00:10:05.620
<i>It's different from Mai's resonance.</i>

00:10:06.880 --> 00:10:09.210
<i>This is more complicated and uncanny.</i>

00:10:09.820 --> 00:10:11.880
<i>What </i>is<i> this sound?</i>

00:10:13.240 --> 00:10:16.110
<i>Nii-chan, this is so frustrating.</i>

00:10:16.110 --> 00:10:17.520
<i>So frustrating!</i>

00:10:40.510 --> 00:10:42.490
I'm heading back to the hotel.

00:10:42.490 --> 00:10:43.070
Huh?

00:10:43.770 --> 00:10:44.750
Fine.

00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:47.690
<i>I want to play the shamisen right now.</i>

00:10:50.080 --> 00:10:51.260
<i>That was...</i>

00:10:52.750 --> 00:10:54.010
<i>...something I want to beat!</i>

00:10:56.520 --> 00:10:59.760
<i>The results announcement
and the awards ceremony</i>

00:10:59.760 --> 00:11:02.140
<i>for the individual
division will begin shortly.</i>

00:11:02.140 --> 00:11:04.720
<i>All participants, please
gather in the performance hall.</i>

00:11:06.700 --> 00:11:08.210
That went really well.

00:11:11.920 --> 00:11:13.620
Sawamura!

00:11:13.620 --> 00:11:15.060
You were amazing!

00:11:15.060 --> 00:11:17.610
I'd expect nothing less
from a friend of mine!

00:11:17.610 --> 00:11:19.610
How do you know my name?

00:11:19.610 --> 00:11:20.820
Mai told me about you.

00:11:21.290 --> 00:11:23.790
You're the grandson of
some guy named Matsugorou.

00:11:23.790 --> 00:11:24.540
So...

00:11:25.110 --> 00:11:28.790
Which half of your performance should
I remember, the first or the second?

00:11:30.020 --> 00:11:30.990
<i>This guy...</i>

00:11:31.240 --> 00:11:33.370
Well, it doesn't matter either way.

00:11:33.800 --> 00:11:37.130
Both were fun. And both...

00:11:37.130 --> 00:11:38.880
...are beatable.

00:11:39.200 --> 00:11:40.240
Bye, then.

00:11:40.240 --> 00:11:40.840
Huh?

00:11:40.840 --> 00:11:43.290
Hey! How was my performance?

00:11:40.840 --> 00:11:43.290
<i>The fact he can flat out
say he'd win is amazing.</i>

00:11:43.290 --> 00:11:44.540
Sawamura!

00:11:44.540 --> 00:11:46.300
<i>He really is amazing.</i>

00:11:49.090 --> 00:11:54.970
<i>Umemaru presents the 1st Annual National
High School Tsugaru Shamisen Koshien:</i>

00:11:54.970 --> 00:11:56.140
<i>the Matsugorou Cup.</i>

00:11:56.160 --> 00:12:00.350
<i>Over the past two days, these high schoolers
have given astonishing performances.</i>

00:11:56.720 --> 00:11:57.900
It's almost time.

00:11:57.900 --> 00:11:58.920
Yup, yup.

00:11:58.920 --> 00:12:02.660
Seems like it'll be a one-on-one duel
with that last guy, Tanuma Souichi, huh?

00:12:00.350 --> 00:12:02.670
<i>But now, things are coming to a close.</i>

00:12:03.150 --> 00:12:05.280
<i>I will now announce the rankings!</i>

00:12:05.280 --> 00:12:06.640
<i>In sixth place...</i>

00:12:06.640 --> 00:12:10.620
<i>From Kougakkan High School of
Ibaraki Prefecture: Tachikawa Shouji-kun!</i>

00:12:11.400 --> 00:12:12.940
<i>In fifth place...</i>

00:12:12.940 --> 00:12:16.480
<i>From Fujiyama High School of
Aichi Prefecture: Takada Nobuto-kun!</i>

00:12:16.480 --> 00:12:17.420
Wakana-chan.

00:12:17.420 --> 00:12:18.210
Huh?

00:12:18.370 --> 00:12:20.070
<i>In fourth place...</i>

00:12:19.240 --> 00:12:21.920
I want to get better. How do I do it?

00:12:20.070 --> 00:12:23.170
<i>From Koutoku High School of
Hokkaido: Fujiwara Jirou.</i>

00:12:23.640 --> 00:12:25.860
Setsu... You...

00:12:26.940 --> 00:12:31.220
It's the reactions of the people listening
that are the most important lessons.

00:12:31.220 --> 00:12:32.680
<i>Gramps.</i>

00:12:32.680 --> 00:12:33.980
<i>Then, why...</i>

00:12:34.260 --> 00:12:35.730
<i>In third place...</i>

00:12:36.030 --> 00:12:40.630
<i>From Umezono Academy of Tokyo:
Sawamura Setsu-kun.</i>

00:12:41.660 --> 00:12:44.830
<i>Sometimes, when you accept the
challenge, it backfires on you.</i>

00:12:44.830 --> 00:12:48.160
Third place! Yay!

00:12:48.160 --> 00:12:49.330
What's going on here?!

00:12:49.330 --> 00:12:51.580
That isn't right! <i>No way</i> is that right!

00:12:51.580 --> 00:12:54.500
Did I choose the wrong time to be happy again?

00:12:54.500 --> 00:12:56.330
L-Let's just have a seat, shall we?

00:12:56.330 --> 00:12:59.090
Huh? Isn't that the guy who
gave that insane performance?

00:12:59.090 --> 00:13:00.970
Yeah, it gave me goosebumps...

00:13:00.970 --> 00:13:02.270
He was only third?

00:13:02.270 --> 00:13:03.630
<i>It was inevitable.</i>

00:13:03.630 --> 00:13:07.000
<i>Sawamura doesn't know how to fight yet.</i>

00:13:03.640 --> 00:13:05.050
<i>In second place...</i>

00:13:05.050 --> 00:13:07.060
<i>From Touhou Academy of
Fukuoka Prefecture:</i>

00:13:07.060 --> 00:13:08.500
<i>Arakawa Ushio-kun!</i>

00:13:09.150 --> 00:13:10.800
Arakawa the genius!

00:13:10.800 --> 00:13:12.490
I am <i>awesome</i>!

00:13:12.490 --> 00:13:15.390
His was fun, sure, but shouldn't
third and second be swapped?

00:13:15.390 --> 00:13:16.970
I disagree with this order.

00:13:16.970 --> 00:13:18.810
Hey! I can hear you over there!

00:13:19.530 --> 00:13:23.450
<i>And now for the winner, who stands
at the peak of the individual division...</i>

00:13:24.120 --> 00:13:25.980
<i>The Matsugorou Award goes to...</i>

00:13:25.980 --> 00:13:28.960
<i>From Aoba Daiichi High School
of Aomori Prefecture:</i>

00:13:28.960 --> 00:13:31.000
<i>Tanuma Souichi-kun!</i>

00:13:33.290 --> 00:13:36.940
<i>Everyone accepts the result.
It's a perfect victory for him.</i>

00:13:38.510 --> 00:13:40.940
<i>If you placed, please make
your way to the stage.</i>

00:13:45.550 --> 00:13:49.360
<i>I see. Setsu already knew how it'd play out.</i>

00:13:49.360 --> 00:13:52.010
No. I just can't accept this.

00:13:52.010 --> 00:13:55.640
For me, Setsu-san had
the winning performance.

00:13:55.640 --> 00:13:58.360
And the audience's reaction was amazing, too.

00:13:58.360 --> 00:14:00.890
How do they score this thing, anyway?

00:14:00.890 --> 00:14:05.560
Yeah. It would've been hard
scoring Setsu's performance.

00:14:05.950 --> 00:14:08.700
<i>In sixth place: Tachikawa Shouji-kun.</i>

00:14:08.990 --> 00:14:10.640
Here you are. Congratulations.

00:14:11.120 --> 00:14:13.120
<i>The judging process was stormy.</i>

00:14:13.390 --> 00:14:14.870
With Sawamura-kun,

00:14:14.870 --> 00:14:18.420
his first and second halves were so
different, it's difficult to judge it.

00:14:19.620 --> 00:14:23.550
But who knew an unknown musician
at that level existed? It's quite a shock.

00:14:23.550 --> 00:14:26.970
He has just as much potential as
Tanuma Souichi of the Kamiki school.

00:14:26.970 --> 00:14:28.380
That's true.

00:14:28.380 --> 00:14:31.390
However, we're not judging
status or potential for growth.

00:14:31.390 --> 00:14:34.680
We must simply evaluate the
performances from this tournament.

00:14:34.680 --> 00:14:38.950
Changing styles mid-performance
reflects negatively in this evaluation.

00:14:34.680 --> 00:14:41.310
Matsugorou Award

00:14:38.950 --> 00:14:41.020
We have no objections to this, do we?

00:14:41.390 --> 00:14:44.560
<i>In third place: Sawamura Setsu-kun.</i>

00:14:41.880 --> 00:14:45.180
<i>Still, he has the same surname as
the organizer of this tournament.</i>

00:14:45.180 --> 00:14:46.650
<i>Is that a coincidence?</i>

00:14:45.180 --> 00:14:49.570
<i>The woman who organized this tournament,
and director of the Umemaru Group,</i>

00:14:49.570 --> 00:14:51.950
<i>Sawamura Umeko-sama
will make the presentation.</i>

00:14:51.950 --> 00:14:52.780
What?

00:14:52.780 --> 00:14:53.820
Uh-oh.

00:14:56.730 --> 00:14:58.000
<i>Umeko?</i>

00:14:58.760 --> 00:15:00.180
Congratulations.

00:15:22.360 --> 00:15:23.980
You're pathetic.

00:15:24.580 --> 00:15:26.320
You've embarrassed me.

00:15:26.940 --> 00:15:29.740
<i>Oh, um, it seems to have
slipped out of her hands.</i>

00:15:29.950 --> 00:15:32.680
<i>Sawamura-kun will
receive his at a later date.</i>

00:15:32.680 --> 00:15:34.830
<i>Please accept our apologies.</i>

00:15:35.240 --> 00:15:36.650
<i>Embarrassed?</i>

00:15:37.270 --> 00:15:39.210
<i>How </i>should<i> I have played?</i>

00:15:40.350 --> 00:15:43.130
<i>I wanted to play Gramps' sound.</i>

00:15:43.130 --> 00:15:45.330
<i>But I'm not Gramps.</i>

00:15:45.330 --> 00:15:48.700
<i>From Aoba Daiichi High School
of Aomori Prefecture:</i>

00:15:45.340 --> 00:15:47.440
<i>I gave it everything I had!</i>

00:15:48.700 --> 00:15:50.340
<i>Tanuma Souichi-kun!</i>

00:15:50.190 --> 00:15:53.180
<i>So what is this emptiness I'm feeling inside?</i>

00:15:56.800 --> 00:15:59.260
598 points?

00:15:59.260 --> 00:16:00.720
Nearly a perfect score...

00:16:00.720 --> 00:16:03.020
He left Sawamura in the dust.

00:16:03.020 --> 00:16:05.520
How do they score this thing, anyway?

00:16:05.520 --> 00:16:06.890
I can't accept this!

00:16:07.590 --> 00:16:08.930
Where's Setsu?

00:16:08.930 --> 00:16:12.740
Changing. On top of where
he placed, <i>that</i> happened,

00:16:13.040 --> 00:16:14.440
Let's give him some time.

00:16:16.940 --> 00:16:19.200
Ah, Sawamura-kun!

00:16:19.470 --> 00:16:20.960
Perfect timing.

00:16:21.210 --> 00:16:25.100
As an alumnus of Umezono Academy,
let me offer you my congratulations.

00:16:25.100 --> 00:16:26.550
Congratulations?

00:16:26.820 --> 00:16:30.630
You placed in your very first
competition. Congratulations.

00:16:30.630 --> 00:16:34.150
This old man came to check out my skills.

00:16:34.150 --> 00:16:36.430
Are you so disappointed
you've got nothing to say?

00:16:37.760 --> 00:16:39.360
I already told you.

00:16:39.360 --> 00:16:41.720
I knew you wouldn't be able to beat Souichi.

00:16:43.370 --> 00:16:45.510
Every little thing's ticking me off!

00:16:45.510 --> 00:16:49.030
You <i>and</i> Umeko! You can just keep
chasing Gramps' ghost forever!

00:16:49.280 --> 00:16:53.150
But will <i>you</i> be able to distance
yourself from Matsugorou?

00:16:53.440 --> 00:16:57.790
Why did you sound so much like Matsugorou
in the first half of your performance?

00:16:57.790 --> 00:16:59.380
Th-That was...

00:16:59.380 --> 00:17:02.030
The way you are now, with no
teacher and no one to help you,

00:17:02.030 --> 00:17:04.910
how do you plan on improving your skills?

00:17:09.650 --> 00:17:10.750
See you around.

00:17:15.130 --> 00:17:18.700
Do you and Ryuugen-sensei
not get along by any chance?

00:17:19.260 --> 00:17:20.980
Silly question, I guess.

00:17:21.550 --> 00:17:26.030
So how did it feel to have a point value
assigned to your playing for the first time?

00:17:26.030 --> 00:17:27.780
To be honest, it made me angry.

00:17:28.170 --> 00:17:29.560
Angry?

00:17:29.560 --> 00:17:31.860
In this world, there is no final goal.

00:17:31.860 --> 00:17:34.620
But those guys decided on a ranking.

00:17:34.620 --> 00:17:39.580
And it's not like any of those judges
understood the sounds I played.

00:17:39.580 --> 00:17:44.860
You gave a wonderful performance, but there
was a huge point gap between you and Souichi.

00:17:44.860 --> 00:17:45.540
Know why?

00:17:47.010 --> 00:17:54.190
Because it didn't matter to the judges if it
was Master Matsugorou's sound or your own.

00:17:54.190 --> 00:17:57.550
What they needed was a cohesive
thread throughout your sound.

00:17:57.980 --> 00:18:00.420
You suddenly switched threads.

00:18:00.420 --> 00:18:03.500
If your expression changes,
it confuses the listeners.

00:18:03.500 --> 00:18:06.940
You went from an old style to a
contemporary one. One extreme to another.

00:18:07.870 --> 00:18:09.810
Your sound is mercurial.

00:18:10.650 --> 00:18:13.250
I've heard your sound several times now,

00:18:13.250 --> 00:18:16.270
but it took until the second half of today's
performance to hear the real you.

00:18:16.270 --> 00:18:19.440
How were you able to stand
not unleashing it until now?

00:18:21.730 --> 00:18:25.370
For a musician, sound
is an expression of self.

00:18:25.370 --> 00:18:29.670
For this expression, you need
others, too: the listeners.

00:18:30.040 --> 00:18:35.180
Everyone in this world hungers
for a place to express their sounds.

00:18:35.180 --> 00:18:37.430
Do you have that hunger?

00:18:37.430 --> 00:18:39.180
I don't feel it from you.

00:18:39.180 --> 00:18:40.380
I do have it!

00:18:40.380 --> 00:18:43.010
If I didn't, I wouldn't feel so frustrated now!

00:18:43.010 --> 00:18:46.270
You didn't feel that desire
until after you'd finished, did you?

00:18:48.060 --> 00:18:49.140
<i>What is this?</i>

00:18:49.140 --> 00:18:52.970
Until after you heard Souichi's sound
and the results came out, right?

00:18:54.260 --> 00:18:57.740
I don't need lots of people to understand.

00:18:57.740 --> 00:18:58.650
<i>I feel hot.</i>

00:18:58.650 --> 00:18:59.610
Neither did Gramps!

00:18:59.610 --> 00:19:00.610
<i>So hot!</i>

00:19:00.930 --> 00:19:03.870
That's because he was
already a master, wasn't it?

00:19:03.870 --> 00:19:07.490
You, on the other hand,
are just being self-indulgent.

00:19:08.270 --> 00:19:11.060
<i>Self indulgent?</i>

00:19:14.920 --> 00:19:15.970
<i>So hot.</i>

00:19:16.420 --> 00:19:18.190
<i>My hands... My arms...</i>

00:19:18.320 --> 00:19:19.930
Ah, Setsu-san!

00:19:18.730 --> 00:19:19.930
<i>My head.</i>

00:19:20.360 --> 00:19:23.180
I knew you wouldn't be able to beat Souichi.

00:19:23.410 --> 00:19:25.720
<i>What did I come to Tokyo for?</i>

00:19:25.720 --> 00:19:27.170
<i>I'm feeling shaken...</i>

00:19:27.170 --> 00:19:28.840
You've embarrassed me.

00:19:28.840 --> 00:19:31.200
<i>What is this feeling?</i>

00:19:31.900 --> 00:19:36.680
Everyone in this world hungers
for a place to express their sounds.

00:19:36.680 --> 00:19:38.800
Do you have that hunger?

00:19:42.460 --> 00:19:43.620
<i>Rejection...</i>

00:19:47.120 --> 00:19:52.380
<i>Does this mean that I...
that my sound doesn't exist?</i>

00:19:57.340 --> 00:20:00.140
<i>This is my hunger.</i>

00:20:01.080 --> 00:20:03.760
Oh, Setsu-san! There you are.

00:20:03.760 --> 00:20:05.600
Hey, Setsu!

00:20:19.350 --> 00:20:21.900
Spoiled, bratty little kid...

00:20:23.240 --> 00:20:25.290
You're not gonna say anything to him?

00:20:25.290 --> 00:20:27.600
I'd never do anything so uncool.

00:20:36.080 --> 00:20:38.500
Umezono Academy

00:20:38.010 --> 00:20:41.120
What? Sawamura didn't come to school?

00:20:41.120 --> 00:20:43.290
No, he didn't show today.

00:20:43.290 --> 00:20:45.160
I'm worried. After school, let's allвЂ”

00:20:45.160 --> 00:20:45.760
Let's wait.

00:20:45.760 --> 00:20:46.550
What?

00:20:46.860 --> 00:20:49.010
No matter what other people say,

00:20:49.010 --> 00:20:52.560
sometimes you can't move forward until
you've come to terms with things yourself.

00:20:53.660 --> 00:20:54.950
<i>Sawamura...</i>

00:20:54.950 --> 00:20:57.120
<i>It took me a while to decide to do it,</i>

00:20:57.120 --> 00:21:02.070
<i>but I'm gonna get the knee surgery
and give soccer my all again.</i>

00:21:05.070 --> 00:21:08.040
Was coming home really
the best course of action?

00:21:08.440 --> 00:21:10.470
You could've stayed with him.

00:21:13.580 --> 00:21:16.670
It's fine. Even if I'd stayed,
there's nothing I can do.

00:21:17.770 --> 00:21:19.680
Right, Gramps?

00:21:23.170 --> 00:21:26.170
Who is Sawamura-kun?

00:21:26.170 --> 00:21:28.160
My son.

00:21:28.160 --> 00:21:31.080
Is it an issue that I didn't mention that?

00:21:31.080 --> 00:21:33.790
No. Our judgment was fair all the same.

00:21:34.320 --> 00:21:36.390
Did you want him to win?

00:21:36.390 --> 00:21:39.190
Well, of course. But through his own skill.

00:21:39.680 --> 00:21:42.910
His performance wasn't
suitable for a competition.

00:21:42.910 --> 00:21:47.050
But in the future, once that sound has
been polished by many more listeners,

00:21:47.050 --> 00:21:48.330
who knows.

00:21:49.960 --> 00:21:53.080
Trying to motivate that
guy is quite difficult.

00:21:55.370 --> 00:21:56.980
<i>Sawamura-kun.</i>

00:21:56.980 --> 00:21:59.470
<i>Your sound is mercurial.</i>

00:21:59.470 --> 00:22:02.090
<i>If you wish to live in this world,</i>

00:22:02.090 --> 00:22:06.470
Tanukichi Diner

00:22:02.090 --> 00:22:06.470
<i>you need to become good enough to make
people acknowledge that mercurial sound.</i>

00:22:07.980 --> 00:22:10.760
Setsu-san hasn't eaten again.

00:22:16.140 --> 00:22:17.280
Sound.

00:22:19.350 --> 00:22:21.610
Use your own sound to steal it.

00:22:31.070 --> 00:22:34.010
<i>My sound...</i>

00:22:36.750 --> 00:22:41.080
Final
Episode

00:22:36.750 --> 00:22:41.080
Those Snow

00:22:36.750 --> 00:22:41.080
White Notes
